{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1527737-what-will-live","id":1527737,"title":"What will live?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-01T20:05:17-08:00","id":1527737,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What will live?","content":"Hypothetical situation and I apologize if this will bother anyone, if any of the supernaturals existed which ones do you think we could be able to live in relative balance and which ones do you think we should unlive, to smooth things over, and why would you think so? I will let my own opinion later, but first I need organize my thoughts better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T05:04:12-08:00","id":1527768,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters are almost definitely at, or at least very, very close to, the top of the list because while they do usually go for seriously heavy partying when 'off-the-job', they're also extensively dedicated to patrolling the recently deceased &amp; helping them move on.<br /> <br /> Promethean's another one that I think would be relatively high up on the list, though <u>definitely</u> much lower than Sin-Eaters due to the involuntary spreading of Wastelands &amp; Disquiet.<br /> <br /> If we're including Fan-Splats, then Nobles would definitely be at the very top due to them having goals &amp; magics distinctly arrayed around aiding humanity ascend to the best version of itself that can exist. Heck, I'd be completely unsurprised if, in such a world, there was a paramilitary/militia organization dedicated towards helping people train up to become Sworn for Nobles to have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T07:44:18-08:00","id":1527772,"title":"","content":"Okay, starting at the top of the list.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Beasts: I'm going to put the two together because in this regard they are similar, they both feed on human beings, one on blood and the other on fears/traumas, so they are predators of human beings, which doesn't leave much space for conversation, someone might comment that a vampire could provide services to earn blood honestly, or only feed on animals, or only attack individuals of questionable morals and the beasts could satisfy their hunger by basically being a good bogeyman or without harming anyone , but I believe that this would not be enough, even if some could live this way it does not change the fact that they are predators, they hunt humans and that they are time bombs, you never know when one of them will lose control due to hunger and so on. risk an innocent. So, yes, I believe that it would not be possible to live peacefully with these two, the difference is that vampires can theoretically be extinct.<br /> <br /> Uratha: These are a little better than the previous ones, but I still think they would be frowned upon and treated as a different species, so they would at best be treated as wild animals, like wolves and bears are dangerous, but if they stay in the forests are fine, if one crosses the line and hunts humans he is sacrificed. Even if they have their mission, I don't think it would ease the anxieties towards people in general, other than they might not believe it, so I think they would generally be just a little better off than the vampires and beasts being partially tolerable.<br /> <br /> Wizards: Right, if a mage uses a spell in front of someone that person won't even process the use of magic, but for the sake of discussion, let's assume that magic is visible, I don't think that would be acceptable, a mage will be seen as something dangerous, someone who could theoretically blow you up with the snap of a finger, and you can't exactly limit them since mages needs to awaken, so they would be hunted out of fear, I don't blame them, because to be honest I also be too.<br /> <br /> Prometheans: The saddest case, I think the Prometheans could coexist peacefully, they want be human after all, but Disquiet is a very big obstacle as well as a risk, so you can't take risks with then.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters: It's an interesting case, I think they would be accepted in certain circles, even though in general they would still suffer rejection because there would still be one or another Sin-eater with a dubious attitude. So safe, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T08:55:01-08:00","id":1527774,"title":"","content":"The question first has to be rejected as having any categorical moral answer for a number of the splats, for whom it is like asking who we should and should not genocide. Genocide is bad.<br /> <br /> Changelings would probably have the easiest time coming out and integrating into a revealed society. The Mask can be lowered, they have comparatively little predatory drive, their primary foes are also generally harmful to mortal humanity, and the main drive towards their &quot;masquerade&quot; is to avoid rediscovery by Keepers and Huntsmen rather than anything intrinsic.<br /> <br /> Prometheans could likely succeed at coming out, but Disquiet and general prejudice and misunderstanding would quickly render them a distrusted and oppressed outgroup. Society already has a distressing tendency towards victim-blaming when a person is repeatedly the center of unrest even before Disquiet puts its supernatural hand on the scale. Public knowledge of Prometheans would also inevitably birth public knowledge of alchemy, which would grow the incentive towards hunting the Created for the fuel to drive research and implementation.<br /> <br /> The worldbuilding of Mage has already thoroughly provided reasons why mages would not <i>want</i> to come public. The Sleeping Curse aside, mages as a whole marry dangerous amounts of individual power to visionary drives to use them in ways others would doubt and try to hold them back from. Many of their ambitions are easier achieved from secrecy. Most of mage society either implicitly or explicitly exalts the Wise as specially privileged to their power in a way that the sleeping masses cannot be trusted with.<br /> <br /> Demon has heavily built up the cosmological and situational reasons why they would not want to come public. As long as the God-Machine predominates, a demon you can unlive is a demon who slipped up already.<br /> <br /> Vampires and the Begotten have physiological needs that are most easily sated by harming mortal humans. An individual vampire or beast who conducts herself with care could coexist in society, but vampires have good reason to believe that most human societies, if they knew of the truth of most vampires, would sooner or later drive those vampires out, whether in fear, wrath, or self-defense.<br /> <br /> Mummies wield their greatest, most spectacular power shortly after they have risen, the same time during which they are still recovering their Memory and operating on instinct and the demands of the Judges of Death. They can issue death curses and summon meteor strikes, and come from an ancient empire with an authoritarian culture to punish in the name of alien gods. If the world learns the truth of the Arisen, they will erupt in panic and launch a Global War on Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T18:28:24-08:00","id":1528191,"title":"","content":"All the minor splats like the Purified, Sorcerers, psychics, etc. could easily blend in with humans. <br /> <br /> In reality, the World of Darkness is a little crowded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"